                "reply_count": 41,
                "retweet_count": 170,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "As a combat veteran, I\u2019ve once been in the position of a young Army Soldier with limited financial resources. Mismanaging funding for Soldiers\u2019 nutrition is a betrayal of those who sacrifice to defend our freedom. For junior enlisted Soldiers, the $465 monthly flat rate for BAS can make up as much as 18% of their total pay. This misappropriation of funds directly reduces the financial support they rely on for their basic needs. The fact that nearly 50% to 80% of the $225 million collected from Soldiers\u2019 BAS pay last year was redirected elsewhere demands an immediate investigation and swift accountability. We cannot achieve military readiness by robbing those who serve of the resources they\u2019ve been promised.\n\nI trust that Secretary of Defense Pete Hegseth will thoroughly investigate this issue. His leadership and unwavering commitment to our warfighters is evident. Under his guidance, we have a real opportunity to address these oversights and strengthen our armed forces, retention, and lethality.",
